<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Prussia</h1><p class="st-meta">1525 CE – 1701 CE · capital Königsberg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first officially Lutheran state, created in 1525 when the Teutonic Order's grand master turned duke and vassal of Poland.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After defeats by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/state-of-the-teutonic-order">State of the Teutonic Order</a> was reduced to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-prussia">East Prussia</a>. In 1525 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-duke-of-prussia">Grand Master Albert of Brandenburg-Ansbach</a>, advised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Luther</a>, secularised the order's state and, by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-krakow">Treaty of Kraków</a>, did homage to his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-i-the-old">King Sigismund I of Poland</a> as hereditary Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> was the first state to adopt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a> officially. Albert founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-konigsberg">University of Königsberg</a> in 1544 and supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> in German, Polish and Lithuanian. The estates were strong, and the land exported grain through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konigsberg">Königsberg</a>. After Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-frederick-duke-of-prussia">Albert Frederick</a> fell mentally ill, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> ruled as regents and in 1618 inherited the duchy, creating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg-prussia">Brandenburg-Prussia</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Elector <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-william-elector-of-brandenburg">Frederick William, the Great Elector</a>, won full <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-wehlau">Treaty of Wehlau</a> in 1657. Because <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> lay outside the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, his son Frederick crowned himself King in Prussia at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konigsberg">Königsberg</a> in 1701, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-prussia">Kingdom of Prussia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-prussia.jpg" alt="Duchy of Prussia" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: Orange Tuesday · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Ducal_Prussia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1525 CE – 1701 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Königsberg</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Albert, Albert Frederick, Frederick William</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Polish, Lithuanian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a>, <a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ducal Prussia, Herzogtum Preußen, Prusy Książęce</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1613&amp;focus=duchy-of-prussia" aria-label="Duchy of Prussia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5131 305 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Prussia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5451 561L5282 625M5451 561L5451 561M5451 56